# managed by lmde7-fde (roles/aide) — do not edit; edit aide_exclude_paths in
# group_vars/all.yml and re-run aide.yml instead.
#
# Debian's shipped configuration already checks the whole filesystem with the
# maximal attribute set (99_aide_root: "/ 0 Full") and copes with the ESP's
# synthesized FAT inode numbers (98_aide_vfat: "/ =vfat Full-i"). /boot and
# /boot/efi therefore need no rules of their own here — anything we added would
# duplicate a rule that is already as strict as AIDE gets.
#
# What is left is pruning the trees whose churn would drown the report.
# "-<regex> 0" is a non-recursive negative rule (AIDE >= 0.19) with an empty
# restriction: the tree is not descended into at all, so nothing below it can
# be pulled back in by another snippet's rule.
#
# The entries are AIDE regexes anchored at the start of the path, not globs.
{% for path in aide_exclude_paths %}
-{{ path }}$ 0
{% endfor %}
